<title>GERMANY: Dyckerhoff eyes higher sales in 97.</title>
<headline>Dyckerhoff eyes higher sales in 97.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction group Dyckerhoff AG said on Wednesday that it expects to post a 10 percent rise in sales to 3.3 billion marks this year.</p>
<p>Profit developments should continue from last year's levels, the group said in a statement released before a news conference.</p>
<p>In 1996 posted a net profit of 151 million marks after a profit of 148 million marks in 1995.</p>
<p>During the first quarter of 1997 Dyckerhoff's sales surged 35 percent to 561 million marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
